// A tree declared `sorted` (Inputs/river_sorted.ent): the
// rows follow the tree through a node made by a system, one that is
// destroyed and one that changes its parent, and the sums down the tree
// are what they are without the sorting.
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/river_sorted.ent 2>/dev/null \
// RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SORTED
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/river_sorted.ent 2>/dev/null \
// RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SORTED
// The same program with its rows left as they are.
// RUN: sed 's/ tree sorted / tree /' %S/Inputs/river_sorted.ent > %t.ent
// RUN: not grep -q sorted.capacity %t.ent
// RUN: %ent run %t.ent 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PLAIN

// Rows are in the tree's order, though the nodes were spawned upstream
// first: the two without a parent, then the others, each after the node it
// flows into.
// SORTED:      1: lake 5 from 50 at 50
// SORTED-NEXT: 1: sea 11111 from 900 at 0
// SORTED-NEXT: 1: river 11110 from 900 at 20
// SORTED-NEXT: 1: creek 100 from 500 at 500
// SORTED-NEXT: 1: brook 11000 from 900 at 300
// SORTED-NEXT: 1: spring 10000 from 900 at 900
// Children first: the rows from the last down, then those without a
// parent.
// SORTED-NEXT: 1: visit spring
// SORTED-NEXT: 1: visit brook
// SORTED-NEXT: 1: visit creek
// SORTED-NEXT: 1: visit river
// SORTED-NEXT: 1: visit lake
// SORTED-NEXT: 1: visit sea
// A node made by a system and connected: sorted in before the next 'for'.
// SORTED-NEXT: 2: lake 5 from 50 at 50
// SORTED-NEXT: 2: sea 11118 from 900 at 0
// SORTED-NEXT: 2: river 11117 from 900 at 20
// SORTED-NEXT: 2: creek 100 from 500 at 500
// SORTED-NEXT: 2: brook 11000 from 900 at 300
// SORTED-NEXT: 2: pond 7 from 60 at 60
// SORTED-NEXT: 2: spring 10000 from 900 at 900
// SORTED-NEXT: 2: visit spring
// SORTED-NEXT: 2: visit pond
// SORTED-NEXT: 2: visit brook
// SORTED-NEXT: 2: visit creek
// SORTED-NEXT: 2: visit river
// SORTED-NEXT: 2: visit lake
// SORTED-NEXT: 2: visit sea
// The brook is gone, and the archetype was sorted for it: the spring above
// it has lost its edge and is a node without a parent.
// SORTED-NEXT: 3: lake 5 from 50 at 50
// SORTED-NEXT: 3: sea 118 from 500 at 0
// SORTED-NEXT: 3: spring 10000 from 900 at 900
// SORTED-NEXT: 3: river 117 from 500 at 20
// SORTED-NEXT: 3: creek 100 from 500 at 500
// SORTED-NEXT: 3: pond 7 from 60 at 60
// SORTED-NEXT: 3: visit pond
// SORTED-NEXT: 3: visit creek
// SORTED-NEXT: 3: visit river
// SORTED-NEXT: 3: visit lake
// SORTED-NEXT: 3: visit sea
// SORTED-NEXT: 3: visit spring
// The creek flows into the lake.
// SORTED-NEXT: 4: lake 105 from 500 at 50
// SORTED-NEXT: 4: sea 18 from 60 at 0
// SORTED-NEXT: 4: spring 10000 from 900 at 900
// SORTED-NEXT: 4: creek 100 from 500 at 500
// SORTED-NEXT: 4: river 17 from 60 at 20
// SORTED-NEXT: 4: pond 7 from 60 at 60
// SORTED-NEXT: 4: visit pond
// SORTED-NEXT: 4: visit river
// SORTED-NEXT: 4: visit creek
// SORTED-NEXT: 4: visit lake
// SORTED-NEXT: 4: visit sea
// SORTED-NEXT: 4: visit spring
// Parents first: every node one higher than the one it flows into.
// SORTED-NEXT: 5: lake 105 from 500 at 50
// SORTED-NEXT: 5: sea 18 from 60 at 0
// SORTED-NEXT: 5: spring 10000 from 900 at 900
// SORTED-NEXT: 5: creek 100 from 500 at 51
// SORTED-NEXT: 5: river 17 from 60 at 1
// SORTED-NEXT: 5: pond 7 from 60 at 2
// SORTED-NEXT: 5: visit pond
// SORTED-NEXT: 5: visit river
// SORTED-NEXT: 5: visit creek
// SORTED-NEXT: 5: visit lake
// SORTED-NEXT: 5: visit sea
// SORTED-NEXT: 5: visit spring
// SORTED-NOT:  {{.}}

// Rows as spawned; the sums are the same.
// PLAIN:      1: spring 10000 from 900 at 900
// PLAIN-NEXT: 1: creek 100 from 500 at 500
// PLAIN-NEXT: 1: brook 11000 from 900 at 300
// PLAIN-NEXT: 1: lake 5 from 50 at 50
// PLAIN-NEXT: 1: river 11110 from 900 at 20
// PLAIN-NEXT: 1: sea 11111 from 900 at 0
// PLAIN-NEXT: 1: visit spring
// PLAIN-NEXT: 1: visit brook
// PLAIN-NEXT: 1: visit creek
// PLAIN-NEXT: 1: visit river
// PLAIN-NEXT: 1: visit lake
// PLAIN-NEXT: 1: visit sea
// PLAIN-NEXT: 2: spring 10000 from 900 at 900
// PLAIN-NEXT: 2: creek 100 from 500 at 500
// PLAIN-NEXT: 2: brook 11000 from 900 at 300
// PLAIN-NEXT: 2: lake 5 from 50 at 50
// PLAIN-NEXT: 2: river 11117 from 900 at 20
// PLAIN-NEXT: 2: sea 11118 from 900 at 0
// PLAIN-NEXT: 2: pond 7 from 60 at 60
// PLAIN-NEXT: 2: visit spring
// PLAIN-NEXT: 2: visit pond
// PLAIN-NEXT: 2: visit brook
// PLAIN-NEXT: 2: visit creek
// PLAIN-NEXT: 2: visit river
// PLAIN-NEXT: 2: visit lake
// PLAIN-NEXT: 2: visit sea
// Nothing sorted the edges when the brook went: the spring keeps its
// edge to it, has no ancestor, and is visited where the edge puts it.
// PLAIN-NEXT: 3: spring 10000 from 900 at 900
// PLAIN-NEXT: 3: creek 100 from 500 at 500
// PLAIN-NEXT: 3: pond 7 from 60 at 60
// PLAIN-NEXT: 3: lake 5 from 50 at 50
// PLAIN-NEXT: 3: river 117 from 500 at 20
// PLAIN-NEXT: 3: sea 118 from 500 at 0
// PLAIN-NEXT: 3: visit spring
// PLAIN-NEXT: 3: visit pond
// PLAIN-NEXT: 3: visit creek
// PLAIN-NEXT: 3: visit river
// PLAIN-NEXT: 3: visit lake
// PLAIN-NEXT: 3: visit sea
// PLAIN-NEXT: 4: spring 10000 from 900 at 900
// PLAIN-NEXT: 4: creek 100 from 500 at 500
// PLAIN-NEXT: 4: pond 7 from 60 at 60
// PLAIN-NEXT: 4: lake 105 from 500 at 50
// PLAIN-NEXT: 4: river 17 from 60 at 20
// PLAIN-NEXT: 4: sea 18 from 60 at 0
// PLAIN-NEXT: 4: visit pond
// PLAIN-NEXT: 4: visit river
// PLAIN-NEXT: 4: visit creek
// PLAIN-NEXT: 4: visit spring
// PLAIN-NEXT: 4: visit lake
// PLAIN-NEXT: 4: visit sea
// PLAIN-NEXT: 5: spring 10000 from 900 at 900
// PLAIN-NEXT: 5: creek 100 from 500 at 51
// PLAIN-NEXT: 5: pond 7 from 60 at 2
// PLAIN-NEXT: 5: lake 105 from 500 at 50
// PLAIN-NEXT: 5: river 17 from 60 at 1
// PLAIN-NEXT: 5: sea 18 from 60 at 0
// PLAIN-NEXT: 5: visit pond
// PLAIN-NEXT: 5: visit river
// PLAIN-NEXT: 5: visit creek
// PLAIN-NEXT: 5: visit spring
// PLAIN-NEXT: 5: visit lake
// PLAIN-NEXT: 5: visit sea
// PLAIN-NOT:  {{.}}

// Spawned in a `for`, one with an edge and one without (Inputs/
// river_bud.ent): both are in their places when the `for` has ended.
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/river_bud.ent 2>/dev/null \
// RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BUD
// BUD:      1: sea 101
// BUD-NEXT: 1: spring 100
// BUD-NEXT: 2: sea 111
// BUD-NEXT: 2: pool 5
// BUD-NEXT: 2: spring 110
// BUD-NEXT: 2: twig 10
// BUD-NOT:  {{.}}
